# Single Product Page Order System — Implementation Plan

A dedicated guest-like order flow where users can purchase a single product directly from its own landing page (`/single-order-page/[slug]/[id]`) without login or cart.

---

## Resolved Questions

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| Login required? | **No** — guest-like flow, no login needed |
| URL format | **`/single-order-page/[slug]/[id]`** — matches existing product detail route pattern (`/products/[slug]/[id]`) |
| Verification | **OTP** — phone SMS OTP + email OTP, matching guest checkout flow |
| Bulk offers | **Smart display** — group by variation, show tier table per variation |
| Coupons | **Completely disabled** — no coupon field, no coupon logic |
| Stock deduction | Same as regular/guest orders (on order creation) |

---

## Cost Calculation Formula

**Regular / Guest / Admin orders** (existing — unchanged):
```
grandTotal = subtotal - discountTotal - bulkDiscountTotal - comboDiscountTotal
           - cartWideDiscount + effectiveDeliveryAmount + weightExtraCharge
```

**Single-page orders** (simplified — only SKU + bulk):
```
grandTotal = subtotal - skuDiscountTotal - bulkDiscountTotal
           + effectiveDeliveryAmount + weightExtraCharge
```

| Discount Type | Applies to Single Page? |
|---|---|
| SKU-level discount (selling_price → final_unit_price) | ✅ Yes |
| Bulk discount (quantity tiers per SKU) | ✅ Yes |
| Combo discount | ❌ No — requires multiple different products |
| Cart-wide discount | ❌ No — cart concept doesn't apply |
| Coupon discount | ❌ No — explicitly disabled |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The new controller will call `calculateBulkComboDiscounts` from `user_discount.js` but **only use `bulkDiscountTotal`** from the result. `comboDiscountTotal` and `cartWideDiscount` will be forced to `0`. This keeps the shared helper intact while enforcing the single-page discount policy.

---

## Current DB State

- **`orders.order_type`**: `ENUM('regular','guest')` — needs `'single_page'` added
- **`products` table**: Has `slug VARCHAR(255)` with unique index — no new column needed for routing
- **`products` table**: Needs `has_single_product_page TINYINT(1) DEFAULT 0` column added

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Database Schema

#### [MODIFY] Database — `products` table

```sql
ALTER TABLE products ADD COLUMN has_single_product_page TINYINT(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
```

#### [MODIFY] Database — `orders` table

```sql
ALTER TABLE orders MODIFY COLUMN order_type ENUM('regular','guest','single_page') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'regular';
```

> [!NOTE]
> Admin manual orders currently insert as `order_type = 'regular'` with `created_by_admin` flag — no enum change needed for those.

